  "section_notes": "S2 sets a 7% failure ceiling for the 55 °C test, just above Northwind's 6.2% and well above Halcyon's 2.1%, with 24 months for existing models, which lets both pass. S4 replaces a suppression mandate with performance-based testing, which avoids Northwind's cost concern less than Halcyon's but still lets Halcyon avoid the $67/unit cost. S1 reporting and S5 disclosure remain fairly strict, though they expose both companies' unreported incidents."
